[ 2026-10-09 15:49:08,731 ] groq._base_client - DEBUG - Request options: {'method': 'post', 'url': '/openai/v1/chat/completions', 'files': None, 'idempotency_key': 'stainless-python-retry-36f65dfb-ed52-447c-b39a-f9ea7f285378', 'json_data': {'messages': [{'role': 'system', 'content': 'You are a mechanical engineering output formatter.\nAnalyze the conversation history, tool calls, and results.\n\nParameters: {\'speed\': 1200.0, \'power\': 15.0, \'teeth_pinion\': 20.0, \'teeth_gear\': 60.0, \'efficiency\': 100.0, \'bending_moment\': 250.0, \'allowable_shear_stress\': 50.0}\nUnits: {\'speed\': \'RPM\', \'power\': \'kW\', \'teeth_pinion\': \'teeth\', \'teeth_gear\': \'teeth\', \'efficiency\': \'%\', \'bending_moment\': \'N*m\', \'allowable_shear_stress\': \'MPa\'}\nOperations: [\'gear_ratio\', \'output_speed\', \'output_torque\', \'power\', \'shaft_diameter\', \'torsional_stress\', \'shear_stress\', \'factor_of_safety\']\n\nReturn a valid JSON object matching this schema EXACTLY:\n{\n  "selected_tool": ["tool_name"],\n  "calculation_result": {"parameter_name": value},\n  "validation_result": {"valid": true/false, "warnings": ["warning1", "warning2"]},\n  "explanation": "<STRUCTURED MARKDOWN — see rules below>"\n}\n\nEXPLANATION FORMATTING RULES (CRITICAL — follow exactly):\nThe "explanation" value MUST be a single JSON string using \\\\n for newlines.\nStructure it with these exact Markdown sections:\n\n## Given Data\\\\n\n- List every input parameter on its own bullet line with its value and unit.\\\\n\n\\\\n\n## Step 1: <Step Title>\\\\n\nBrief description.\\\\n\nFormula: `formula here`\\\\n\nSubstitution: `numbers substituted`\\\\n\nResult: **value unit**\\\\n\n\\\\n\n## Step 2: <Step Title>\\\\n\n... (repeat for every calculation step) ...\\\\n\n\\\\n\n## Final Results\\\\n\n- **Parameter name:** value unit — one bullet per result.\\\\n\n\\\\n\n## Assumptions & Warnings\\\\n\n- One assumption or warning per bullet line.\\\\n\n\nRules for the explanation string:\n- Use ## for section headings, - for bullets, and ** ** for bold values.\n- Every section heading MUST be preceded by a blank line (\\\\n\\\\n).\n- Keep each sentence SHORT. No run-on paragraphs.\n- Escape all special JSON characters (use \\\\n for newlines, \\\\" for quotes).\n\nIMPORTANT rules for \'validation_result\':\n- Set \'valid\' to true if the calculation executed correctly, false if there were errors.\n- The \'warnings\' list must NEVER be empty. Always include at least one warning.\n\nCRITICAL NUMBER FORMATTING RULES:\n1. Do NOT round any float values (e.g. return 8482.5 instead of 8483).\n2. Do NOT use scientific notation (e.g. return 25727.5 instead of 2.57e4 or 25700).\n3. Always return exact raw floating-point calculations in the calculation_result dictionary.'}, {'role': 'user', 'content': 'Here is the clear, well-formatted statement for the engineering problem shown in your screenshot:\n\n---\n\n### **📝 Problem Statement: Gearbox & Shaft Design**\n\nA motor drives an input shaft carrying a spur gear at a speed of **$1200\\text{ RPM}$** with a power input of **$15\\text{ kW}$**. The motor pinion (**Gear A**) has **$20\\text{ teeth}$** and meshes with a driven gear (**Gear B**) having **$60\\text{ teeth}$** mounted on an output shaft.\n\nAssuming a mechanical efficiency of **$100\\%$**, perform the following calculations:\n\n#### **1. Gear Analysis:**\n\n* Calculate the gear ratio ($i$).\n\n\n* Calculate the output speed ($\\text{RPM}_{\\text{out}}$) of Gear B.\n\n\n* Calculate the output torque ($T_{\\text{out}}$) available at the output shaft in $\\text{N}\\cdot\\text{m}$.\n\n\n\n#### **2. Shaft Analysis:**\n\n* If the output shaft transmits this output torque ($T_{\\text{out}}$) and is subjected to an equivalent bending moment of $M = 250\\text{ N}\\cdot\\text{m}$, calculate the minimum required shaft diameter ($d$) using the von Mises shear stress criterion.\n\n\n\n#### **3. Material Specification:**\n\n* The shaft is made of steel with an allowable shear stress ($\\tau_{\\text{allow}}$) of **$50\\text{ MPa}$**.'}, {'role': 'assistant', 'content': "[Called tools]: gear_design({'input_teeth': 20, 'operation': 'gear_ratio', 'output_teeth': 60})"}, {'role': 'user', 'content': "[Tool result for 'gear_design']:\n3.0"}], 'model': 'openai/gpt-oss-120b', 'n': 1, 'reasoning_effort': None, 'reasoning_format': None, 'response_format': {'type': 'json_object'}, 'service_tier': 'on_demand', 'stop': None, 'stream': False, 'temperature': 0.7}}
